msgid "Open in debug mode"
msgstr "Öppna i debugläge"

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "A view from the ESO headquarters in Garching bei Munchen, Germany."
msgstr "En vy från ESO-högkvarteret i Garching bein München, Tyskland."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Horizon line of Geneva. Sample to show compatibility with the format used by <a href=\"http://www.ap-i.net/skychart/en/start\">Cartes du Ciel</a>, taken with permission from <a href=\"http://sourceforge.net/p/skychart/code/HEAD/tree/trunk/tools/data/horizon/horizon_Geneve.txt\">here</a>."
msgstr "Genèves horisontlinje. Ett exempel för att visa kompatibiliteten med formatet som används av <a href=\"http://www.ap-i.net/skychart/en/start\">Cartes du Ciel</a>, taget med tillstånd <a href=\"http://sourceforge.net/p/skychart/code/HEAD/tree/trunk/tools/data/horizon/horizon_Geneve.txt\">här</a>."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Field next to the Leeberg (Hallstatt-era giant tumulus, 16m) at Grossmugl, Lower Austria, primary observing Spot of the Grossmugl Starlight Oasis near Vienna."
msgstr "Fält bredvid Leeberg (Hallstatt-era giant tumulus, 16m) vid Grossmugl, Niederösterreich, observerplats för Grossmugl Starlight Oases, när Wien."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Despite its vicinity to a large city, light pollution is concentrated mostly on the southern horizon, and the Milky Way is well visible if a bit higher in the sky.  In the eastern horizon, red lights indicate a wind park also at night.  <a href=\"https://starlightoasis.org\">https://starlightoasis.org</a>."
msgstr "Trots sin belägenhet nära en storstad är ljusföroreningarna mestadels koncentrerade till den södra horisonten, och Vintergatan syns tydligt om den står högre upp på himlen. Vid horisonten i öster syns under natten röda ljus från vindkraftsparken.  <a href=\"https://starlightoasis.org\">https://starlightoasis.org</a>."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Guéreins"
msgstr "Guéreins"

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Guéreins is a small French village in the Valley of the Saône river, 50 km North of Lyon. In the west stand the small mountains of the \"Beaujolais\" where the famous wine is produced. It is also the town where Stellarium was born :)"
msgstr "Guéreins är en liten fransk by belägen i Saônedalen, 50 km norr om Lyon. I väster finns de små bergen Beaujolais, där det kända vinet produceras. Detta är också platsen där Stellarium föddes. :)"

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "An edited view from Hurricane Ridge in Olympic National Park, Washington. In reality there is an expansive view of the rest of the Olympic range to the South but lighting conditions were poor."
msgstr "En redigerad vy från Hurricane Ridge i Olympic National Park i delstaten Washington. I verkligheten syns bergskedjan Olympic bättre, men ljusförhållandena var dåliga när detta panorama togs."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Simple Jupiter gas surface (\"top of atmosphere\")"
msgstr "Ett enkelt landskap som visar toppen av Jupiters atmosfär."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "The panoramic camera on NASA's Mars Exploration Rover Spirit took the hundreds of images combined into this 360-degree view, the \"Husband Hill Summit\" panorama. The images were acquired on Spirit's sols 583 to 586 (Aug. 24 to 27, 2005), shortly after the rover reached the crest of \"Husband Hill\" inside Mars' Gusev Crater."
msgstr "Mars Exploration Rover Spirit tog hundratals bilder med sin panoramakamera, som kombinerades till denna 360-gradersvy. Panoramat kallas \"Husband Hill Summit\". Bilderna insamlades under Spirits sol 583 till 586 (24-27 augusti 2005), kort efter att roboten nådde krönet till Husband Hill, mitt i Gusevkratern på Mars."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Photo taken from Apollo 17 Mission"
msgstr "Foto taget under Apollo 17-uppdraget."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Simple Neptune gas surface (\"top of atmosphere\")"
msgstr "Ett enkelt landskap som visar toppen av Neptunus atmosfär."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Made with Terragen."
msgstr "Skapades med Terragen."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Simple Saturn gas surface (\"top of atmosphere\")"
msgstr "Ett enkelt landskap som visar toppen av Saturnus atmosfär."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Simple Sun gas surface (\"top of photosphere\")"
msgstr "Ett enkelt landskap som visar toppen av solens fotosfär."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Trees in Greenlake Park, Seattle"
msgstr "Träd i Greenlake Park, Seattle."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "Simple Uranus gas surface (\"top of atmosphere\")"
msgstr "Ett enkelt landskap som visar toppen av Uranus atmosfär."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-stellarium-landscapes-descriptions-pot--master
msgid "A simple polygonal landscape that just covers the area below the mathematical horizon."
msgstr "Ett enkelt polygonlandskap som endast visar den del av himlen som befinner sig ovanför den matematiska horisonten."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-metainfo-stellarium-metainfo-pot--master
msgid "Desktop Planetarium"
msgstr "Skrivbordsplanetarium"

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-metainfo-stellarium-metainfo-pot--master
msgid "Stellarium renders 3D photo-realistic skies in real time with OpenGL. It displays stars, constellations, planets and nebulae, and has many other features including multiple panoramic landscapes, fog, light pollution simulation and a built-in scripting engine."
msgstr "Stellarium renderar fotorealistiska 3D-himlar i realtid med OpenGL. Det visar stjärnor, stjärnbilder, planeter och nebulosor, och har många andra funktioner inklusive flera panoramalandskap, dimma, simulering av ljusförorening och en inbyggd skriptmotor."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-metainfo-stellarium-metainfo-pot--master
msgid "Stellarium comes with a star catalogue of about 600 thousand stars and it is possible to download extra catalogues with up to 220 million stars."
msgstr "Stellarium levereras med en stjärnkatalog med ca 600 000 stjärnor och det är möjligt att hämta ner extrakataloger med upp till 220 miljoner stjärnor."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-metainfo-stellarium-metainfo-pot--master
msgid "Stellarium has multiple sky cultures - see the constellations from the traditions of Polynesian, Inuit, Navajo, Korean, Greek and Chinese astronomers, as well as the traditional Western or official modern constellations."
msgstr "Stellarium har flera himmelskulturer - se konstellationer från traditionerna hos polynesiska, inuitiska, navajo-, koreanska, grekiska och kinesiska astronomer, liksom de traditionella västerländska eller officiella moderna konstellationerna."

#. from transifex:stellarium-stellarium-po-stellarium-metainfo-stellarium-metainfo-pot--master
msgid "It is also possible to visit other planets in the solar system - see what the sky looked like to the Apollo astronauts, or what the rings of Saturn looks like from Titan."
msgstr "Det är också möjligt att besöka andra planeter i solsystemet - se hur himlen såg ut för astronauterna på Apollo, eller hur Saturnus ringar ser ut från Titan."

